<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Włocławek</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Włocławek is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, in the historical region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a>. From the 12th century it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Kuyavia, whose Gothic cathedral still dominates the town. It grew as a river port and grain-trading centre and later became an industrial town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wloclawek.jpg" alt="Włocławek" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aneta Pawska · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bazylika_katedralna_WNMP_we_W%C5%82oc%C5%82awku,_widok_z_drona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
